2026-11-01T08:18:49.5344083Z === Feature modules ===
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5344700Z   ok   keystone: _expire_away_override returns the live override's (True, return time) and a lapsed one's (False, None), saving only the lapse
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5345079Z 
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5345210Z -- Input staleness watchdog (item 12)
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5345471Z   ok   a fresh sensor reads normally
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5345862Z   ok   an over-age value is rejected
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5346160Z   ok   the rejected value is still available for a graceful fallback
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5346483Z   ok   the age is reported so a user can see why
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5346791Z   ok   an outdoor reading may be older than an indoor one
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5347086Z   ok   the watchdog can be switched off entirely
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5347343Z   ok   the age limit can be relaxed
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5347612Z   ok   a future-stamped state is stale, not age 0
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5347926Z   ok   a 4 h backward host-clock step flags the reading stale
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5348225Z   ok   unavailable is distinguished from stale
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5348499Z   ok   a missing entity is reported as such
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5348766Z   ok   an unconfigured input is not a problem
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5349025Z   ok   a non-numeric state does not raise
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5349335Z   ok   a non-finite state string is refused exactly like a word
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5349677Z   ok   a non-finite value is refused after unit conversion too
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5350124Z   ok   the °F path itself keeps working (null control for the guard above)
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5350501Z   ok   an untimestamped state is used rather than discarded
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5350793Z   ok   stale inputs are listed
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5351119Z   ok   missing inputs are listed
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5351404Z   ok   the summary is human-readable
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5351647Z   ok   the evidence names the entity
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5351889Z   ok   the failing entity ids are listed
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5352181Z   ok   each failure reads as one line naming entity and class
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5352456Z   ok   watts are converted to kW
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5352667Z   ok   kilowatts pass through
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5353005Z   ok   an unrecognised unit is refused rather than guessed
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5353283Z   ok   a missing unit is refused
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5353623Z   ok   a power state parses to finite kW under the caller's sign policy, or to no reading
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5353999Z   ok   a power entity is normalised on read
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5354308Z   ok   a wrongly-united power entity yields nothing
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5354681Z   ok   an unknown unit reads as words, not a token
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5355128Z   ok   every word-valued failure class renders in words a user can read
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5355686Z   ok   an unconfigured slot contributes no source and no line
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5356088Z   ok   a °F temperature is converted to °C on read
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5356405Z   ok   the DHW tank's °F reading converts exactly
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5356697Z   ok   a Wh energy meter is converted to kWh on read
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5357017Z   ok   a kelvin reading is converted to °C on read
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5357324Z   ok   a °C state still reads bit-for-bit
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5357648Z   ok   an unrecognised unit keeps today's raw read instead of a guess
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5357861Z 
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5358093Z -- R9 N-clamp-range: the flow-lift bias reaches the plant's supply (D2-s2-02)
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5358588Z   ok   D2-s2-02: a 50 C plant against the model's curve is priced at 50 C, not pinned 15 K over the curve
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5359177Z   ok   D2-s2-02: the bias still stops FLOW_BIAS_CLAMP_K under the curve
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5359640Z   ok   D2-s2-02: a supply no direct plant runs at (degF adopted raw) is refused as a sample, not absorbed
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5360194Z   ok   D2-s2-02: a plant at the supply ceiling is learned all the way up
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5360685Z   ok   D2-s2-02: a stored bias this version learns loads as stored; a wild one is re-clamped to the supply ceiling
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5361288Z   ok   D2-s2-02: a restored bias at the ceiling prices no supply past FLOW_SUPPLY_MAX_C on the coldest curve
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5361940Z   ok   D2-s2-02: the supply ceiling is 75 C, so an 80 C measured supply is refused as a sample
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5362561Z   ok   D2-s2-02: on a curve above the ceiling the hot-side bound is zero, not negative: a positive bias lands at 0 and the cold clamp still holds
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5363177Z   ok   D2-s2-02: a non-finite outdoor temperature prices no curve flow at all
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5363446Z 
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5363770Z -- R9 N-future-instant: a persisted instant ahead of the clock (FI-sw1, FI-sw2, FI-sw3, FI-sw4, FI-rca1)
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5364474Z   ok   FI-sw1: a fuse-advisor stamp ahead of the clock, inside its month, does not hold the 7-day cooldown past it; an honest recent stamp still does
2026-11-01T08:18:49.5365375Z   ok   FI-sw2: a heavy-snow stamp ahead of the clock does not keep the damping on 30 days later; an honest day-old stamp still does
